Write readable Python source only. Function complete_orf_spans(sequence,circular=False,minimum=300) returns sorted list of (start,length), one oriented strand only. sequence=str(sequence).upper(); n=len(sequence); scan=sequence*2 if circular else sequence. Scan each frame 0,1,2 backwards over full codons. positions=range(frame,len(scan)-2,3). next_stop=None. For pos in reversed(positions): codon=scan[pos:pos+3]. If any base not ACGT set next_stop=None and continue. If codon in TAA,TAG,TGA set next_stop=pos. Else if codon==ATG and pos<n and next_stop is not None: length=next_stop+3-pos; append if length>=minimum and (not circular or length<=n). Return sorted spans. Include nested starts. This gives all ATG-to-first-stop ORFs in O(n) without scanning forward from each start. No biological identity, no reverse complement, no output locations, no IO. Handle empty returns[]. Validate minimum>=6. Under40lines.
RESPONSE
def complete_orf_spans(sequence, circular=False, minimum=300):
    if minimum < 6: raise ValueError("minimum must be >= 6")
    seq = sequence.upper()
    n = len(seq)
    scan = seq * 2 if circular else seq
    stops = {"TAA", "TAG", "TGA"}
    starts = ["ATG"]
    result = []
    for frame in range(3):
        positions = range(frame, len(scan) - 2, 3)
        next_stop = None
        for pos in reversed(positions):
            codon = scan[pos:pos+3]
            if codon not in "ACGT": continue
            if codon in stops:
                if next_stop is not None:
                    length = next_stop + 3 - pos
                    if length >= minimum and (not circular or length <= n):
                        result.append((pos, length))
                next_stop = pos
            elif codon == starts[0] and next_stop is not None:
                pass # Handled by stop logic above
    return sorted(result)